From: skornuta <126527569+skornuta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:32:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/27] Detile ring trim (VICTORY_GPU_DETILE_TRIM=1, off):
 small rings outside bursts

The GPU detile's rings (512 + 512 MB in play.ps1) are for loading; in
the world they hold a few MB at most, and both take the process's
commit (the card's ring its memory too) for the whole run.

With the switch the rings shrink to VICTORY_GPU_DETILE_SMALL_MB each (64)
once no upload has wanted more for VICTORY_GPU_DETILE_TRIM_S seconds
(20), and grow back to their full sizes when one does: an upload of more
than a quarter of the small rings, rings filled past half of them, or an
upload refused for room. A resize is made at a submission that detiles
nothing, only with both rings empty (nothing reserved, nothing waiting
for the card; a list holds its uploads until its reset, so no list
submitted again can still read a ring), no checks or jobs pending and
the detile lists run; the old rings go behind the running submissions
(`retire`). An upload the rings cannot take meanwhile is detiled on the
CPU, as every refused one is.

The memory CSV gets the rings shrunk and grown back.

(cherry picked from commit 390d949a3eeec2387abf85f48a1a5792c1c741b8)
